I hate to beat a dead horse, but I am still a bit concerned about
this dog/ring of conflict stuff.

If I understand this part right, there are two things that increase about a
little dog, size AND level.  i.e. you can have a little dog that is seventh
level.  I know this is true, because I have had this situation.  I repeat,
I KNOW this is how it was.

As I understand it(which is shakey at best), a dog increases in size when
he eats enough, and level when he kills enough.  right???

OK, so here is the rub.  When I was wearing a ring of conflict my little 
dog(this is a fact), who was third level(this is also a fact) attacked
a minotaur.  He, of course, died fast, but he did attack.  I repeated this
many times(at least 7), and he did it each time. When I did not have the
ring on, he did not attack.  The way that I could test this was that I was in
Wiz mode, and I probed the dog every time I made one.  The only way to avoid
saying the ring caused his attack would be to say that the fact I was a Wiz
did it.  If this is true, then I am wrong, and the ring of conflict did not
cause him to attack.  But if my Wiz-ness had nothing to do with it, then what
other explanation could there be?  Does anyone out there(preferably those
on the dev team, like Kenneth, or someone with more wiz experience) have
any ideas on this?


By the way, how can one make a little dog that is first level in Wiz mode???

Thanks for your responses.

